# Changelog
All notable changes to the skin3d library will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [0.2.0] - 2026-08-08

**Minor Release: Performance Optimizations, Memory Leak Fixes, and Rendering Improvements**

### Added
- ✨ **Material quality presets**: New `MaterialType` option for performance/quality tradeoff
  - `"standard"`: `MeshStandardMaterial` (PBR, better lighting, slower)
  - `"lambert"`: `MeshLambertMaterial` (flat Gouraud shading, faster)
  - Available in `PlayerObject`, `SkinObject`, `CapeObject`, `ElytraObject`, and `EarsObject` constructors
  - Backward compatible with default `"standard"` behavior

- ✨ **Pixel ratio control**: New `maxPixelRatio` property on `Render` class
  - Allows clamping device pixel ratio to improve performance on high-DPI displays
  - Helps reduce rendering overhead on 4K/5K displays

### Fixed
- ✅ **Critical memory leak fixes**: Comprehensive resource cleanup in `Render.dispose()`
  - Proper disposal of name tag textures and materials
  - Complete cleanup of player object meshes (geometry + materials)
  - Disposal of FXAA pass materials, shaders, and composer render targets
  - Proper removal of event listeners (mousedown, mouseup, touchmove, touchend)
  - Cleanup of camera and scene lights

- ✅ **Race condition guards**: Added ID-based tracking for async load operations
  - Prevents visual glitches when multiple skin/cape/ears/background loads occur in quick succession
  - Ensures only the latest load request is applied
  - Applied to `loadSkin()`, `loadCape()`, `loadEars()`, and `loadBackground()` methods

- ✅ **Null safety improvements**: Removed non-null assertions in `NameTagObject`
  - Added proper null checks for canvas 2D rendering context
  - Throws descriptive error if context cannot be obtained

### Changed
- 🔧 **Code quality improvements**: Enhanced type safety and documentation
  - Fixed TSDoc formatting with consistent `@param` style using dashes
  - Fixed broken markdown link in `NameTagObject` documentation
  - Improved null handling in `nameTag` setter with proper disposal of old name tags
  - Added null check for FXAA pass uniform updates

- 🔧 **File header consistency**: Changed file headers from `/**` to `/*` format

---

## [0.1.2] - 2026-01-04

**Patch Release: Build Fixes and Configuration Updates**

### Fixed
- ✅ **Resolved TypeScript build error TS1261**: Fixed file casing mismatch between `model.ts` and import statements
  - Updated imports in `src/Animation.ts`, `src/index.ts`, and `src/skin3d.ts` from `./Model.js` to `./model.js`
  - This resolved the "Already included file name differs only in casing" error on Windows systems
  
- ✅ **Updated Rollup configuration**: Added missing external dependencies to prevent build warnings
  - Added `skinview-utils` and three.js example modules to external dependencies list
  - Added corresponding global variable mappings for UMD bundle format

### Changed
- 🔧 **Build system improvements**: Enhanced rollup.config.ts with complete external dependency declarations
- 🔧 **Cross-platform compatibility**: Fixed case-sensitivity issues for Windows development environments

---

## [0.1.0] - 2025-12-31

**Major Release: Refactored Library with Enhanced Documentation**

### Added
- ✨ **Modular Architecture**: Refactored library structure with separated concerns
  - New `Render.ts` class replacing the previous `skin3d.ts` - Core rendering engine for 3D player models using Three.js
  - New modular structure with separate `index.ts` entry point for cleaner exports
  - Refactored module exports: `Model.ts`, `Render.ts`, `Animation.ts`, `Nametag.ts`

- 📚 **Comprehensive Documentation Suite** (8 documentation files, 3,200+ lines)
  - GETTING_STARTED.md - Installation, setup, and framework integration (React, Vue, Svelte)
  - EXAMPLES.md - 10+ practical code examples
  - API_REFERENCE.md - Complete API documentation with all classes and methods
  - ARCHITECTURE.md - Library design, structure, and design patterns
  - ADVANCED_USAGE.md - Performance optimization, custom animations, and extensions
  - MIGRATION_GUIDE.md - Upgrade path from previous versions
  - TROUBLESHOOTING.md - Common issues and solutions
  - README.md - Documentation index and overview

- 🧹 **Dependency Cleanup**
  - Removed unused npm polyfills (path, url)
  - Optimized production bundle size
  - Improved tree-shaking with named exports

### Changed
- 🔄 **Breaking Change:** Main class renamed from `View` to `Render`
  - Updated all imports and examples to use new name
  - Added migration guide for upgrading from v0.0.10

- 📦 **Enhanced Module Structure**
  - Refactored library structure from monolithic entry point to modular component exports
  - Updated file naming convention (capitalized: `Animation.ts`, `Model.ts`, `Nametag.ts`, `Render.ts`)
  - Modified project dependencies in `package.json` to support new architecture

- 📖 **Improved README**
  - Added recent changes section
  - Updated code examples with named imports
  - Added comprehensive documentation section
  - Added breaking changes notice with migration guide link

### Fixed
- ✅ Corrected background image path in app.css
- ✅ Improved error handling in documentation loading

### Removed
- Legacy `skin3d.ts` entry point (functionality moved to `Render.ts`)
- Legacy `view.ts` file
- Removed `demo/` folder (no longer part of main library distribution)
- Removed `docs/` static folder (now generated dynamically)
- Unused npm dependencies (path, url polyfills)

---

## [0.0.10] - Previous Release

